# Run-wide default anomalies of the L3 verifier (spec/harness.md "L3",
# spec/plumb.md §10.2): what a reference linker does on essentially every
# link of a kind, so no test declares it. One line per default:
#
#   <linker>[,<more linkers or architectures>]: <id>...
#
# A defaulted anomaly is expected on every judged output of that linker
# (and architecture), and the run fails if it is found on none of them.
# mortar never has a default. Anything else a test meets it declares
# with `#@ anomaly(<linker>): <id>...`, under the strict rule both ways.

# mold: its canonical IFUNC symbols and their aliases (A1, A2, from the
# C runtime's IFUNCs), its _TLS_MODULE_BASE_ (A3) and the globals it makes
# local in a static executable's .symtab (A9). The -nostdlib links see
# only A3 and A9, the glibc driver links all four.
mold: A1 A2 A3 A9

# GNU ld: the labels crtbegin/crtend put on sections the link leaves
# empty (`__TMC_END__` and kin) - on every driver link with the C runtime.
# Not seen on any i386 output (WP-028e).
bfd,aarch64,x86_64: A10

# mold on x86-64: the 8-aligned .note.gnu.property and the 4-aligned
# notes after it (ABI tag, package, build id) share one PT_NOTE with
# p_align 8 (A13), on every link with the cross C runtime's notes. Only
# the cross one (`cross`: x86-64 off an x86-64 host): its crt1.o has a
# .note.package whose size is not a multiple of 8, so the notes after it
# are misread under p_align 8; the native crt1.o (Debian's libc6-dev on
# an x86-64 host) has no .note.package, every note then falls on 8, and
# the same PT_NOTE reads right (WP-015).
mold,x86_64,cross: A13
